---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — VatSnap"
  description="VatSnap privacy policy: no accounts, no tracking, no cookies. Calculations run in your browser; hosting logs only."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    VatSnap is a static calculator. There is nothing to sign up for, and
    nothing to track you with. Last updated: September 2026.
  </p>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Short version</h2>
    <p>
      We do not collect, store, or sell personal data. Calculations happen
      entirely in your browser — the prices you type never leave your device.
    </p>
    <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts, no names, no email addresses.</li>
      <li>No advertising trackers, no third-party cookies.</li>
      <li>No server-side storage — there is no database behind this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use privacy-friendly, aggregate measurement (Google Analytics) to see
      which pages are visited, so we know what to improve. It does not track
      the prices you type into the calculator — those never leave your device.
      You can block it with any content blocker and the site keeps working.
    </p>
    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your theme preference (light/dark) is saved in your browser's
      <code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>vatsnap-theme</code> so the
      site remembers it. Nothing else is stored, and clearing site data removes
      it. No cookies are set by VatSnap itself.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting &amp; infrastructure</h2>
    <p>
      VatSnap is hosted on Cloudflare (Workers static assets). Like any host,
      Cloudflare may process basic technical logs (e.g. IP address, requested
      URL, timestamps) to deliver pages securely and prevent abuse. We do not
      have access to per-visitor analytics beyond what Cloudflare provides by
      default, and we do not combine any such data with anything else —
      because there is nothing else.
    </p>
    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>
      The site loads fonts from Google Fonts. When your browser fetches them,
      Google receives a standard web request (similar to loading any file from
      a CDN). If you prefer, you can block third-party font requests — the
      site still works with system fonts.
    </p>
    <h2>Embedded widget</h2>
    <p>
      If you embed the VatSnap widget (<code>/embed/</code>) on your own site,
      the same rules apply: the widget runs client-side and sends nothing back
      to us.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you email us, we will only use your address to reply. See our
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes, the updated version will be posted here with
      a new "last updated" date.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
